<title>USA: Movie Star Q4 shr loss narrows to $0.07.</title>
<headline>Movie Star Q4 shr loss narrows to $0.07.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr    loss		$0.07     loss	 $0.38</p>
<p> Net    loss		1,020     loss	 5,264</p>
<p> Revs			14,059		   16,182</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,960		   13,960</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr    loss		$0.38     loss	 $0.38</p>
<p> Net    loss		5,278     loss	 5,029</p>
<p> Revs			84,115		  101,946</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  13,960		   13,960</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Period ended June 30.</p>
<p>Full Company name is Movie Star Inc.</p>
<p>The company said the fourth quarter 1996 decline in sales was due to the popular priced intimate apparel line, and reflected management's decision to elimate low margin trade business from its sales mix and continued sourcing problems.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it consolidated its New York city offices to reduce overhead expenses, and closed seven under-utlized domestic factories over the past year.</p>
</text>
